# DECISIONS.md - the ADR log

Append-only entries below, index on top. The bar for an entry: the decision must
outlive its spec or cross spec boundaries; a choice fully contained in one spec
lives in that spec file (the ADR economy, framework Part 4). Never silently
reverse a decision: supersede it with a new entry and flip the index row.
The Status column uses Part 4's legend and nothing else: ACTIVE,
SUPERSEDED-by-NNN, or INFERRED (retrofit-seeded, pending the flip ceremony).

## Index

| ID | Decision (one line) | Status |
|---|---|---|

[PHASE 2 SLOT: the founding ADRs (typically five: stack, core data model, scope
boundary, working mode, and the framework adoption itself), each as an index row
above and a full entry below.]

